Build ccv and NNC into one shared library

Adds cc_shared_library ccv_nnc_shared, rooted at @ccv's nnc and ccv targets
plus @sqlite3's implementation, with soname libccv_nnc.so, and a cc_import and
a ccv_nnc_dynamic interface over it. The four ccv-backed shims C_ccv, C_nnc,
C_sqlite3 and C_sfmt redirect to it, so a consumer links one copy of the CUDA
fatbin and the ccv host code instead of one per binary. The sqlite root is
there because Store.swift opens handles that ccv_nnc_tensor_read consumes, and
one copy processwide is the only arrangement that works.

Retention of the transitive sub-libraries rides on alwayslink in @ccv rather
than on this rule, because cc_shared_library whole-archives only its direct
deps.
